        "body": "Philippines staffing can extend coverage, but a time-zone difference does not repair an unclear queue. Define which hours need live attention, which requests can wait, and which event contacts an onshore owner. The assistant’s final handoff should state what changed, what remains unresolved, the linked source, the deadline, and the next owner. Keep urgent exceptions separate from a long narrative update. Test the handoff on a normal day and on a day with an absence, system outage, or unusual volume. Name backup coverage and the source it should use rather than assuming someone will notice an abandoned queue. Confirm that the next person acknowledges high-impact work so sending a message is not mistaken for transferring responsibility."
